📘 Outbooked
Outbooked is a structured, responsive event management system built using ASP.NET Core Razor Pages and Bootstrap 5. It provides full CRUD support, real-time conflict detection, simulated Outlook syncing, and unit test coverage—all powered by an in-memory data store ideal for demo environments.

🚀 Features
- ✅ Create, edit, delete, and view events via Razor Pages
- 🔁 Conflict detection via TripleSeatService
- 🔗 Mock Outlook sync via OutlookSyncService (expandable to Graph API)
- 💬 Toast-based feedback for user actions
- 🏷️ Status badges for event filtering (Confirmed, Pending, Cancelled, Synced)
- 📐 Clean homepage layout with CTA and subtle styling
- 🧪 Unit tests with xUnit in a dedicated Outbooked.Tests project

🧱 Tech Stack
| Layer | Tools & Frameworks | 
| Backend | C#, Razor Pages (.NET 8), Dependency Injection | 
| Services | EventRepository, TripleSeatService, OutlookSyncService | 
| UI / UX | Razor Pages, Bootstrap 5, Toast notifications | 
| Testing | xUnit with logic validation and mock simulation | 
| Environment | Visual Studio, .NET SDK | 

🧰 Setup Instructions
- Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/OutbookedApp
- Open the solution in Visual Studio
- Set Outbooked.Web as the startup project
- Run the app and navigate to /Events
- Sample data is preloaded via EventRepository—no database required

🧪 Testing Overview
The Outbooked.Tests project includes unit tests for:
- ✅ Conflict detection logic in TripleSeatService
- ✅ Edge case handling for overlapping and adjacent events
- ✅ Sync simulation validation in OutlookSyncService
Run tests via Visual Studio Test Explorer. All tests are isolated and deterministic.

